Python tutorial: plotting the twisted cubic with Matplotlib
***********************************************************

In this tutorial, we use Matplotlib (see https://matplotlib.org/ ) to plot the
twisted cubic in three different ways.  We are assuming that Matplotlib is
already installed.  See *note pipInstall: pipInstall, to learn how to install
Python modules.

This example is heavily inspired by the Parametric curve (see
https://matplotlib.org/stable/gallery/mplot3d/lines3d.html ) example in the
matplotlib documentation.

Running Python code directly
============================

If we just want to run some Python code directly, then the simplest way is with
the *note pythonRunScript: pythonRunScript, method.

For this example, we have our code saved as a .py file.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : pycode = get(Python#"auxiliary files" | "doc/matplotlib-example.py")   |
|                                                                            |
|o1 = import matplotlib.pyplot as plt                                        |
|     import numpy as np                                                     |
|                                                                            |
|     fig = plt.figure()                                                     |
|     ax = fig.add_subplot(projection='3d')                                  |
|     t = np.linspace(-10, 10, 100)                                          |
|     ax.plot(t, t**2, t**3)                                                 |
|     plt.show()                                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
