pythonValue -- execute Python source code from a string
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        pythonValue s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or a *note sequence:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, containing Python source code;
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Global => a *note python object: PythonObject,, default value null,
        globals dictionary;
  * Outputs:
      * a *note python object: PythonObject,, the return value of the given
        code;

Description
===========

This function a is wrapper around the function PyRun_String (see
https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/veryhigh.html#c.PyRun_String ) from the Python
C API.

+------------------------------+
|i1 : pythonValue "2 + 2"      |
|                              |
|o1 = 4                        |
|                              |
|o1 : PythonObject of class int|
+------------------------------+

If a sequence is given, then its elements are converted to strings using *note
toString: (Macaulay2Doc)toString, and then joined using *note concatenate:
(Macaulay2Doc)concatenate,.  You can see the expression sent to the Python
interpreter by setting *note debugLevel: (Macaulay2Doc)debugLevel, to a
positive value.

+------------------------------+
|i2 : debugLevel = 1           |
|                              |
|o2 = 1                        |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : x = 5                    |
|                              |
|o3 = 5                        |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : pythonValue("3 + ", x)   |
| -- python command: 3 + 5     |
|                              |
|o4 = 8                        |
|                              |
|o4 : PythonObject of class int|
+------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note runSimpleString: runSimpleString, -- execute Python source code from
    a string in __main__
  * *note pythonRunScript: pythonRunScript, -- execute a sequence of Python
    statements

Ways to use pythonValue:
========================

  * "pythonValue(Sequence)"
  * "pythonValue(String)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note pythonValue: pythonValue, is a *note method function with a
single argument: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionSingle,.

