pythonRunScript -- execute a sequence of Python statements
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        pythonRunScript s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or a *note sequence:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, containing Python code;
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Global => a *note python object: PythonObject,, default value null,
        globals dictionary;
  * Outputs:
      * a *note python object: PythonObject,, the globals dictionary; 

Description
===========

Execute a sequence of statements as if they were read from a Python file. This
is for multi-line code that might contain definitions, control structures,
imports, etc.  It is great for running Python code from a file.

The return value is a Python dictionary containing all the variables defined in
the global scope.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : pyfile = temporaryFileName() | ".py"                          |
|                                                                   |
|o1 = /tmp/M2-54590-0/0.py                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : pyfile << "import math" << endl                               |
|                                                                   |
|o2 = /tmp/M2-54590-0/0.py                                          |
|                                                                   |
|o2 : File                                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : pyfile << "x = math.sin(3.4)" << endl << close                |
|                                                                   |
|o3 = /tmp/M2-54590-0/0.py                                          |
|                                                                   |
|o3 : File                                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : get pyfile                                                    |
|                                                                   |
|o4 = import math                                                   |
|     x = math.sin(3.4)                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : pythonRunScript oo                                            |
|                                                                   |
|o5 = {'math': <module 'math' (built-in)>, 'x': -0.2555411020268312}|
|                                                                   |
|o5 : PythonObject of class dict                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

The Global option may be used to pass a globals dictionary so that variables
may be shared between scripts.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : pythonRunScript("y = math.cos(x)", Global => oo)                   |
|                                                                        |
|o6 = {'math': <module 'math' (built-in)>, 'x': -0.2555411020268312, 'y':|
|     0.9675266635316214}                                                |
|                                                                        |
|o6 : PythonObject of class dict                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note pythonValue: pythonValue, -- execute Python source code from a string
  * *note runSimpleString: runSimpleString, -- execute Python source code from
    a string in __main__

Ways to use pythonRunScript:
============================

  * "pythonRunScript(Sequence)"
  * "pythonRunScript(String)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note pythonRunScript: pythonRunScript, is a *note method function
with a single argument: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionSingle,.

