setupVirtualEnvironment -- set up a virtual environment
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        setupVirtualEnvironment dir
  * Inputs:
      * dir, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 

Description
===========

This sets up a Python virtual environment.  It is equivalent to calling python3
-m venv dir on the command line.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : dir = applicationDirectory() | "venv"|
|                                          |
|o1 = /home/profzoom/.Macaulay2/venv       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : setupVirtualEnvironment dir          |
+------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

To use the virtual environment, you must restart Macaulay2 and then load the
Python package with the "executable" configuration option set to point to the
Python executable in dir.

