import -- import a Python module
********************************

  * Usage: 
        import s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, the name of a python module; 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note python object: PythonObject,, the imported module; 

Description
===========

This is a wrapper around the Python C API function PyImport_ImportModule (see
https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/import.html#c.PyImport_ImportModule ) and
returns an imported Python module.

Once imported, the statements and definitions from the module are available
using *note PythonObject @@ Thing: PythonObject @@ Thing,.

+---------------------------------+
|i1 : math = import "math"        |
|                                 |
|o1 = <module 'math' (built-in)>  |
|                                 |
|o1 : PythonObject of class module|
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : math@@pi                    |
|                                 |
|o2 = 3.141592653589793           |
|                                 |
|o2 : PythonObject of class float |
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : math@@sqrt 2                |
|                                 |
|o3 = 1.4142135623730951          |
|                                 |
|o3 : PythonObject of class float |
+---------------------------------+

