value(PythonObject) -- convert python objects to Macaulay2 things
*****************************************************************

  * Function: *note value: (Macaulay2Doc)value,
  * Usage: 
        value x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note python object: PythonObject,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, the Macaulay2 equivalent of x; 

Description
===========

This function attempts to convert x to its corresponding Macaulay2 equivalent.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : value pythonValue "[1, 3.14159, 'foo', (1,2,3), {'foo':'bar'}]"|
|                                                                    |
|o1 = {1, 3.14159, foo, (1, 2, 3), HashTable{"foo" => bar}}          |
|                                                                    |
|o1 : List                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : class \ oo                                                     |
|                                                                    |
|o2 = {ZZ, RR, String, Sequence, HashTable}                          |
|                                                                    |
|o2 : List                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

Since the type of x is not initially known, a sequence of *note hooks:
(Macaulay2Doc)using hooks, are used to determine its type and then convert it.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : hooks value                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {0 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {1 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {2 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {3 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {4 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {5 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {6 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {7 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {8 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {9 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {10 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : NumberedVerticalList                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|unknown -> PythonObject)                    }                                |
|collections.abc.Callable -> FunctionClosure)}                                |
|collections.abc.Mapping -> HashTable)       }                                |
|collections.abc.Set -> Set)                 }                                |
|collections.abc.Sequence -> Sequence)       }                                |
|collections.abc.MutableSequence -> List)    }                                |
|str -> String)                              }                                |
|numbers.Complex -> CC)                      }                                |
|numbers.Real -> RR)                         }                                |
|numbers.Integral -> ZZ)                     }                                |
| bool -> Boolean)                           }                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If no conversion can be done, then x is returned.

Users may add additional hooks using *note addHook: (Macaulay2Doc)addHook, or
the convenience function *note addPyToM2Function: addPyToM2Function,.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note value(PythonObject): value_lpPythonObject_rp, -- convert python
    objects to Macaulay2 things
