addPyToM2Function -- convenience function for adding value hooks
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        addPyToM2Function(type, f, desc)
  * Inputs:
      * type, a *note python object: PythonObject,, a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, or a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the
        type(s) to convert;
      * f, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, the function that will do
        the converting;
      * desc, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, passed to the Strategy
        option of *note addHook: (Macaulay2Doc)addHook,;

Description
===========

Most of the hooks used by *note value: (Macaulay2Doc)value, have the same
general format: if the python object has a particular type, then use a
particular function to convert it to a corresponding Macaulay2 thing.  This
function simplifies the process of adding such a hook.

For example, suppose we would like to convert Fraction objects from the Python
fractions (see https://docs.python.org/3/library/fractions.html ) module to
*note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ, objects.  Without adding a hook, *note value:
(Macaulay2Doc)value, will convert these objects to *note RR: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,
objects.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : fractions = import "fractions"                              |
|                                                                 |
|o1 = <module 'fractions' from '/usr/lib/python3.12/fractions.py'>|
|                                                                 |
|o1 : PythonObject of class module                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : x = fractions@@"Fraction"(2, 3)                             |
|                                                                 |
|o2 = 2/3                                                         |
|                                                                 |
|o2 : PythonObject of class fractions.Fraction                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : value x                                                     |
|                                                                 |
|o3 = .6666666666666666                                           |
|                                                                 |
|o3 : RR (of precision 53)                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

So we write a function to do the conversion and then install the hook using
addPyToM2Function.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : toQQ = x -> value x@@"numerator" / value x@@"denominator";              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : addPyToM2Function("fractions.Fraction", toQQ, "Fraction -> QQ");        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : value x                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|     2                                                                       |
|o6 = -                                                                       |
|     3                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : QQ                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : hooks value                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = {0 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {1 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {2 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {3 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {4 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {5 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {6 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {7 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {8 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {9 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                 |
|     {10 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                |
|     {11 => (value, PythonObject, Strategy =>                                |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : NumberedVerticalList                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|unknown -> PythonObject)                    }                                |
|collections.abc.Callable -> FunctionClosure)}                                |
|collections.abc.Mapping -> HashTable)       }                                |
|collections.abc.Set -> Set)                 }                                |
|collections.abc.Sequence -> Sequence)       }                                |
|collections.abc.MutableSequence -> List)    }                                |
|str -> String)                              }                                |
|numbers.Complex -> CC)                      }                                |
|numbers.Real -> RR)                         }                                |
|numbers.Integral -> ZZ)                     }                                |
| bool -> Boolean)                           }                                |
| Fraction -> QQ)                            }                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

