toString(PythonObject) -- readable string representation of a python object
***************************************************************************

  * Function: *note toString: (Macaulay2Doc)toString,
  * Usage: 
        toString x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note python object: PythonObject,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 

Description
===========

This is equivalent to Python's builtin str function.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : datetime = import "datetime"                              |
|                                                               |
|o1 = <module 'datetime' from '/usr/lib/python3.12/datetime.py'>|
|                                                               |
|o1 : PythonObject of class module                              |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : epoch = datetime@@"datetime"(1970, 1, 1)                  |
|                                                               |
|o2 = 1970-01-01 00:00:00                                       |
|                                                               |
|o2 : PythonObject of class datetime.datetime                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : toString epoch                                            |
|                                                               |
|o3 = 1970-01-01 00:00:00                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that *note expression: (Macaulay2Doc)expression,, *note net:
(Macaulay2Doc)net,, and *note texMath: (Macaulay2Doc)texMath, do essentially
the same thing, but return an *note Expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Expression,, a
*note Net: (Macaulay2Doc)Net,, or a string for use in TeX code, respectively.

+---------------------------------+
|i4 : expression epoch            |
|                                 |
|o4 = 1970-01-01 00:00:00         |
|                                 |
|o4 : Expression of class Holder  |
+---------------------------------+
|i5 : net epoch                   |
|                                 |
|o5 = 1970-01-01 00:00:00         |
+---------------------------------+
|i6 : texMath epoch               |
|                                 |
|o6 = \texttt{1970-01-01 00:00:00}|
+---------------------------------+

