|                                    |
|o4 = false                          |
+------------------------------------+

When used with dictionaries, which are Python's equivalent of Macaulay2 hash
tables, the keys are tested for membership.  In this sense, it is like the
Macaulay2 *note #?: (Macaulay2Doc)#?, and *note .?: (Macaulay2Doc)_pd?,
operators.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isMember("foo", toPython hashTable {"foo" => "bar"})|
