PythonObject ^^ PythonObject -- bitwise exclusive disjunction of Python objects
*******************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^^: (Macaulay2Doc)^^,
  * Usage: 
        x ^^ y
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note python object: PythonObject,, 
      * y, a *note python object: PythonObject,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note python object: PythonObject,, bitwise exclusive disjunction of
        x and y;

Description
===========

Perform the bitwise exclusive disjunction ("xor") operation on Python objects.

+------------------------------+
|i1 : toPython 6 ^^ toPython 3 |
|                              |
|o1 = 5                        |
|                              |
|o1 : PythonObject of class int|
+------------------------------+

If one of the arguments is a Macaulay2 object, then it is first converted to a
Python object.

+------------------------------+
|i2 : toPython 14 ^^ 7         |
|                              |
|o2 = 9                        |
|                              |
|o2 : PythonObject of class int|
+------------------------------+
|i3 : 14 ^^ toPython 7         |
|                              |
|o3 = 9                        |
|                              |
|o3 : PythonObject of class int|
+------------------------------+

Caveat
======

In Python, the ^ operator corresponds to the bitwise xor operation. We use ^^
in this case for consistency with the rest of Macaulay2. The ^ operator is used
for exponentiation.

