PythonContext -- persistent Python execution environment
********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        new PythonContext
        PythonContext s
        ctx s
  * Inputs:
      * ctx, a *note Python context: PythonContext,, 
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Python context: PythonContext,, 

Description
===========

The class PythonContext represents a persistent Python execution environment
that maintains its own global namespace. It allows you to evaluate Python
expressions and statements across multiple calls, preserving defined variables
and imports.

When a PythonContext object is created, the given string is executed as Python
code within a new global context.  Subsequent calls evaluate additional Python
code in the same context, allowing variables and imports to persist.

Each evaluation returns a *note PythonObject: PythonObject, representing the
result of the final expression in the string, if any.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : math = PythonContext "from math import *"|
|                                              |
|o1 = math                                     |
|                                              |
|o1 : PythonContext                            |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : math "x = sin(3.4)"                      |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : math "sin(3.4)"                          |
|                                              |
|o3 = -0.2555411020268312                      |
|                                              |
|o3 : PythonObject of class float              |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : math "x"                                 |
|                                              |
|o4 = -0.2555411020268312                      |
|                                              |
|o4 : PythonObject of class float              |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : math "e"                                 |
|                                              |
|o5 = 2.718281828459045                        |
|                                              |
|o5 : PythonObject of class float              |
+----------------------------------------------+

Here, the import from the Python math module is performed once during
initialization.  The variable x remains available in subsequent calls to the
same PythonContext instance.

* Menu:

* PythonContext _ String: PythonContext _us String.  get value of variable in a python context
* listSymbols(PythonContext): listSymbols_lpPythonContext_rp.  get a table of all the variables and their values in a python context
* use(PythonContext): use_lpPythonContext_rp.  install variables from a python context

Methods that use a Python context:
==================================

  * *note listSymbols(PythonContext): listSymbols_lpPythonContext_rp, -- get a
    table of all the variables and their values in a python context
  * "new PythonContext"
  * "new PythonContext from String"
  * "PythonContext String"
  * *note PythonContext _ String: PythonContext _us String, -- get value of
    variable in a python context
  * *note use(PythonContext): use_lpPythonContext_rp, -- install variables from
    a python context

For the programmer
==================

The object *note PythonContext: PythonContext, is a *note self initializing
type: (Macaulay2Doc)SelfInitializingType,, with ancestor classes *note
MutableHashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)MutableHashTable, < *note HashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

